tes, I saw Canada,” says U.S. Representative Debbie Dingell (D-MI). CFR visited the Michigan-Ontario corridor to convene senior-level public and private officials for discussions on U.S.-Canada trade relations. We https://t.co/RTZ09h4eM9", "url": "https://x.com/CFR_org/status/2120246666003361954"}, {"author_id": "272019676", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:00:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120245164866208148"], "id": "2120245164866208148", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1399, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "On October 29, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney unveiled the country’s first national security strategy in over 20 years. CSIS experts explore what’s in the new plan, why is it being issued now, and how is the U.S. likely to view the Canadian government’s strategy?\n\nRead:", "url": "https://x.com/CSIS/status/2120245164866208148"}, {"author_id": "60783724", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:44:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120241153312256186"], "id": "2120241153312256186", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 20, "impression_count": 22965, "like_count": 372, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 52, "retweet_count": 39}, "text": "jensen huang told president trump he had no idea his lady friend was a chinese spy. that’s credible. \n\nbut why wouldn’t trump—or anyone in the administration—have told jensen when they had the information? when it would have been a national security concern of the highest level.", "url": "https://x.com/ianbremmer/status/2120241153312256186"}, {"author_id": "17469492", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:21:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120235393677189133"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/mpA3kDUxkv", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/CFR_org/status/2120235393677189133/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120235255827210240", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/mpA3kDUxkv"}]}, "id": "2120235393677189133", "public_metrics": {"bookmar